23,2,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The late-turn pool is dangerously thin, and we're relying on overtime for everything. However, the lift maintenance contract actually has spare capacity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Eight years ago, a contactless payment trial worked perfectly, and a late-evening pilot hit its cost targets. But some old lane-priority stretches failed.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Pre-war shells are a nightmare; bidders are pricing in huge contingencies because of unrecorded voids. Also, ferry and rail back offices can't agree on data.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The capital ledger has a lapsed grant balance, but the technology line was trimmed. Ticketing fees are now higher than our paving budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Mid-city runs are slower than they used to be, but the crowds clear at the same rate. Most delays are actually waiting for connections!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, if the late-evening pilot was successful, do we have the staff to actually do it now?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"I don't know about now, but the record shows the idea itself is sound.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, if the technology budget is trimmed, we should be wary of any complex new software systems.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. I'm worried about the long-term costs of these contracts.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, if the lift crews are available, maybe we should focus on station movement?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, that's a good point. But the late-turn pool is so depleted that any extension of hours would be a huge risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, if the pre-war shells are unpredictable, any deep station work is probably going to blow the budget.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Exactly. The ground is hiding things that the drawings don't show.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Sakura, you said the delays are in the connections, not the ticketing. Does that mean a new fare system wouldn't help?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"It might not fix the waiting time, but it could make the transition smoother!","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Victoria,,We need to avoid anything that drains the remaining crew energy.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Takumi,,And we should avoid repeating the lane-priority mistakes of the past.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I suspect any project involving the ferry and rail data integration will stall in committee.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I just want something that doesn't create a financial burden we can't handle later.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm just thinking about the passengers waiting on those platforms!,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
