49,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"The candidates are A: Bus Corridor, B: Night Service, C: Station Access, and D: Fare Platform. I lean toward C.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"B had a successful pilot, but A's lane-priority has a history of failure. I'm considering B or D.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Toshio,,A and C involve physical risks—roadworks and pre-war shells. D has data agreement issues. B is the cleanest.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,D's ticketing fees are already a problem. B seems... less likely to require a massive new capital outlay.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Sakura,,B helps the people waiting late at night! But C helps the flow. I'm torn between B and D.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, you think B is cleanest, but my roster data shows the late-turn pool is empty. B is impossible without new hires.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, that's a fair point. If the staff aren't there, the plan is just a piece of paper.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"If B is a staffing risk and C is a structural risk, we must look at D, despite the committee friction.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"But @Toshio, the technology budget was trimmed. Can we even afford D?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, maybe the lapsed grant Victoria mentioned could be used? Wait, Daisuke mentioned the grant!","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Victoria,,C uses the lift maintenance capacity I found. It's the only plan that aligns with our current available manpower.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"C is risky because of the ""voids"" Toshio found in the shells. It could stall for weeks.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"True. D is a bureaucratic struggle, but it doesn't involve digging holes in pre-war basements.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think D is too expensive. C is safer if we use the existing maintenance contract.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"If the mid-city runs are slow, A would help, but Takumi said lane-priority fails. I'll go with C!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I'm sticking with C. It's the most rational use of the available crew.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'll vote for B. The pilot proved it works, and we can solve the staffing later.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I cannot support C or A. I vote for D.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for C. It feels the least risky for the budget.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm voting for C too! Let's fix the stations.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
